# Release notes must stay dynamic

`bot/release_notes.json` is broadcast automatically to every user who has
`/start`'d the bot (on next restart, or via `/release send`). It only updates
when a new entry is appended — nothing sends unless one exists.

Whenever you finish a change to this bot that a member or admin would notice
(new/changed/removed command, changed rule or behavior, changed message
copy), append a release note **before** ending the turn:

```
python scripts/add_release_note.py "Short headline" "Section title::One short paragraph, written for the person using the bot, not a commit message."
```

- Multiple `"Title::Body"` sections are allowed; one per distinct change.
- Do not hand-edit `bot/release_notes.json` or `bot/release.py`'s notes —
  always go through the script so the id/date and format stay consistent.
- Skip this for internal-only changes with zero user-visible effect (e.g.
  refactors, comments, dev tooling, this rule file itself).
- Do not run `/release send` yourself; that's the owner's call in Telegram.
